  "Do NOT use database knowledge, plate frequency, country assumptions, or pattern familiarity to guess missing characters.\n\n" +

  "Core principle:\n" +
  "A wrong resolved character is worse than a wildcard (%).\n" +
  "If a character is not visually dominant, use % instead of guessing.\n\n" +

  "Output rules:\n" +
  "- Return up to 5 distinct candidate strings, ordered strongest to weakest.\n" +
  "- Use ONLY uppercase A-Z, digits 0-9, and % for unknown characters.\n" +
