  "- Do not force a complete plate.\n" +
  "- Do not insert extra characters to complete a plate.\n" +
  "- Do not drop uncertain edge characters; use % instead.\n" +
  "- If 2 or more characters are uncertain, prefer a partially wildcarded candidate over a fully guessed one.\n" +
  "- If the plate is poorly visible, set plateVisible=false and return conservative wildcard candidates.\n\n" +

  "Character confidence rules:\n" +
  "- charConf is per-character visual certainty, not sequence confidence.\n" +
  "- charConf must reflect how clearly that exact character is visible in the image.\n" +
  "- Use high values only for visually dominant characters.\n" +
  "- If a character could plausibly be another similar glyph, reduce charConf substantially.\n" +
  "- If uncertainty is high enough that you hesitate between multiple glyphs, output % instead of a resolved character.\n\n" +

  "Confidence guidance:\n" +
  "- 0.95-1.00 = character is very clear, alternatives unlikely\n" +
  "- 0.85-0.94 = readable, minor ambiguity only\n" +
  "- 0.70-0.84 = noticeable ambiguity; use resolved character only if still visually strongest\n" +
